{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016T8xA1Cx18HaGDzJnFPyUE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: \"Reframe 不降级目标（仍冲 EMNLP），但从 'finding paper' 转向 'methodology + diagnostic framework' contribution。核心 claim 从 'severity is strategy×phase emergent' 收缩为 'compound interaction exhibits phase-dependent heterogeneity that standard evaluation misses'。Phase gradient 作为 robust phenomenon 保留（importance 内部 d_z>1.0 跨所有模型始终成立），strategy specificity 降级为 'one manifestation that varies by context'。Practical hook：phase-stratified audit protocol + open-source toolkit。Related Work 定位为 complementary to Physics of KV Cache。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"c1_bf16_importance_s025\"\n    plan_id: \"c1_bf16_importance_s025\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek importance masking s025 phase gradient\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_high_median: 0.032\n      ii_mid_median: 1.12\n      ii_low_median: 7.20\n      median_difference: 7.16\n      gradient_direction: \"monotonic increasing\"\n    result_rationale: \"Importance 内部 phase gradient 在 worst tier 下依然成立——这是 robust phenomenon。问题不在 importance 本身的 gradient，而在于 random 也可能表现出类似 gradient（尤其在 LLaMA 架构上），导致 strategy specificity 被质疑。DeepSeek s025 importance 数据本身不受 worst tier 影响，因为 worst 的核心打击点是跨架构/跨 benchmark 的 strategy 区分度消失，不是 importance gradient 本身消失。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: [\"Phase gradient bar chart 仍显示 low>>mid>>high，但 reviewer 会注脚 'also observed in random on LLaMA'\"]\n    analysis: \"数据本身 PASS，但 worst tier 解读为 'phase gradient is universal phenomenon not specific to importance strategy'——需在论文中预防性承认这一解读可能性。\"\n\n  - name: \"c1_bf16_ds_rand_s025\"\n    plan_id: \"c1_bf16_ds_rand_s025\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek random masking s025 — flat gradient baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_high_median: 0.82\n      ii_mid_median: 0.93\n      ii_low_median: 1.36\n      median_difference: 0.54\n      pass_fail: \"FAIL (flat)\"\n    result_rationale: \"DeepSeek random 在 s025 确实 flat——但 worst tier 的攻击点是：(1) LLaMA random 不 flat（d_z 0.35-0.44），(2) GPQA 上 importance/random ratio 可能趋近 1.0。所以即使 DS random s025 flat，reviewer 可以论证这仅是 architecture-specific 而非 universal property of randomness。Random 在某些架构上也有 phase gradient → strategy specificity 不是 fundamental distinction 而是 contingent observation。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"FAIL verdict 表面支持 strategy specificity，但 LLaMA 数据否定了这一结论的普适性。\"\n\n  - name: \"c1_bf16_qw_imp_s025\"\n    plan_id: \"c1_bf16_qw_imp_s025\"\n    description: \"Qwen cross-model replication importance s025\"\n    expected_results:\n      median_difference: 1.11\n      cohens_d: 1.23\n      permutation_p: 0.0\n    result_rationale: \"Qwen importance gradient 在 worst tier 下同样 robust——两个 Qwen2 架构模型一致。但 reviewer 解读：'两个模型共享 Qwen2ForCausalLM 架构，不是独立验证。LLaMA 上效应弱化证明 architecture 是 confound'。Cross-model 变成 'same-architecture replication' 而非 'generalization evidence'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"数值强，但被框定为 architecture-specific phenomenon 的重复测量而非独立泛化。\"\n\n  - name: \"c1_sf5_asymmetric_spot\"\n    plan_id: \"c1_sf5_asymmetric_spot\"\n    description: \"Asymmetric head/KV configs\"\n    expected_results:\n      config_a_D: 19.13\n      config_b_D: 18.25\n      gradient_consistent: true\n    result_rationale: \"Asymmetric configs 仍显示 gradient——worst tier 不否认 DeepSeek 上 compound interaction 存在 phase modulation。攻击点转移至：'yes compound interaction is phase-modulated on DeepSeek Qwen2 architecture, but this is architecture-specific, not fundamental'。Ablation 变成 'thorough characterization of one architecture' 而非 'generalizable finding'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Passes criterion but scope-limited in worst tier framing.\"\n\n  - name: \"c1_c2_accuracy_eval\"\n    plan_id: \"c1_c2_accuracy_eval\"\n    description: \"Accuracy degradation across sparsity levels\"\n    expected_results:\n      ds_dense_acc: 0.52\n      ds_s030_acc: 0.10\n      ds_s030_delta: -0.42\n      qw_s030_acc: 0.14\n      qw_s030_delta: -0.18\n    result_rationale: \"Accuracy 大幅下降不被争议——compound sparsity 有 practical impact 是共识。Worst tier 攻击的不是 'compound sparsity hurts' 而是 'whether the phase×strategy interaction is the useful framing'。Reviewer: 'Everyone knows compound compression hurts. The question is whether your phase-stratified analysis adds actionable insight beyond what aggregate metrics already show—and your mitigation pilot failed'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Accuracy eval 本身不受 worst tier 影响，但 'so what' 质疑加强——因为 mitigation 未成功。\"\n\n  - name: \"c2_bf16_importance_s030\"\n    plan_id: \"c2_bf16_importance_s030\"\n    description: \"Phase gradient at highest sparsity\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 14.64\n      ii_high_median: 0.053\n      low_high_ratio: 276\n      median_difference: 14.59\n    result_rationale: \"S030 importance gradient 极强（276×），worst tier 不否认这个数字。但 reviewer 框架：'Large effect at extreme sparsity (30% heads pruned) is unsurprising—of course severe compression interacts with everything. The interesting question is whether this is strategy-specific, and your LLaMA data + GPQA data suggest it's not'。效应量大但 novelty 消失。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Strong numbers, weak novelty interpretation in worst tier.\"\n\n  - name: \"c2_v6_importance_s030\"\n    plan_id: \"c2_v6_importance_s030\"\n    description: \"v6 pipeline s030 results\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 34.69\n      ii_high_median: 0.88\n      bootstrap_gradient: 41.92\n    result_rationale: \"V6 pipeline 数字更大（不同 II 定义），但同样面临 'so what' 问题。Worst tier 下 reviewer 说 'these large numbers reflect your specific II metric definition, not necessarily a practically meaningful phase interaction. The metric itself is not validated against downstream task performance beyond the failed mitigation pilot'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Metric validity questioned without successful downstream application.\"\n\n  - name: \"c2_think_phase_validation\"\n    plan_id: \"c2_think_phase_validation\"\n    description: \"Phase segmentation alignment with think/answer\"\n    expected_results:\n      median_kappa: 0.887\n      thinking_in_low_sparsity: 0.578\n      answer_in_high_sparsity: 0.627\n    result_rationale: \"Phase segmentation 与 think/answer 对齐度中等（57.8%/62.7%），worst tier 解读：'Phase segmentation only partially aligns with semantic phases—42% of thinking tokens end up in high-sparsity phase. This imperfect alignment weakens the mechanistic story because the \"phases\" are statistical artifacts of sparsity distribution, not semantic constructs'。Kappa 0.887 看似高但是 adaptive threshold 产物。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Reviewer questions whether 'phases' have semantic meaning beyond statistical convenience.\"\n\n  - name: \"c2_acc_qw_s030_n100\"\n    plan_id: \"c2_acc_qw_s030_n100\"\n    description: \"Qwen s030 accuracy n=100\"\n    expected_results:\n      combined_acc: 0.19\n      batch_effect: \"batch1=14% vs batch2=24%\"\n    result_rationale: \"Batch effect (14% vs 24%) 在 worst tier 被放大：'10pp batch variation on n=50 suggests high measurement noise. Combined 19% vs dense 46% confirms degradation, but the variance raises questions about reproducibility of finer-grained phase-level measurements'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Batch variability undermines confidence in fine-grained per-phase claims.\"\n\n  - name: \"c2_acc_ds_s015_8k_v2\"\n    plan_id: \"c2_acc_ds_s015_8k_v2\"\n    description: \"DS s015 accuracy with 8k token limit\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.48\n      truncation_rate: 0.32\n      non_truncated_accuracy: 0.706\n    result_rationale: \"32% truncation rate 在 worst tier 是 confound：'16 of 50 problems were truncated at s015, which conflates compression-induced degradation with generation length limitation. Non-truncated accuracy (70.6%) suggests most degradation comes from truncation, not phase-dependent compound interaction'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Truncation confound weakens accuracy as supporting evidence for phase-dependent severity.\"\n\n  - name: \"c3_v6_importance_s025\"\n    plan_id: \"c3_v6_importance_s025\"\n    description: \"Crossover evidence — importance phase gradient\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 24.16\n      ii_high_median: 0.66\n      ratio: 36\n    result_rationale: \"Crossover claim 在 worst tier 被重新解读：'At s025, importance high_phase (0.032) < random (0.818) while importance low_phase (7.196) > random (1.363). But this \"crossover\" requires comparing importance vs random—if strategy specificity doesn't generalize (LLaMA, GPQA), the crossover is just an artifact of comparing two things that behave similarly on other architectures'。Crossover 依赖 strategy specificity 成立。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Crossover claim logically depends on strategy specificity; if specificity is architecture-specific, crossover is too.\"\n\n  - name: \"c3_v6_random_s025\"\n    plan_id: \"c3_v6_random_s025\"\n    description: \"Random flat at s025 — crossover baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 2.91\n      ii_high_median: 3.00\n      bootstrap_p: 0.559\n      verdict: \"FAIL (flat)\"\n    result_rationale: \"V6 random s025 flat (bootstrap_p=0.559) 在 DeepSeek 上支持 crossover。Worst tier 反驳：'Random is flat on DeepSeek at s025 but NOT on LLaMA (d_z 0.45 at s025, CI excludes zero). The flatness of random is architecture-dependent, so the crossover phenomenon is also architecture-dependent. On LLaMA, both strategies show phase gradient → no meaningful crossover'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Architecture-dependence of random behavior invalidates universality of crossover.\"\n\n  - name: \"c3_bf16_importance_s020\"\n    plan_id: \"c3_bf16_importance_s020\"\n    description: \"Importance at moderate sparsity\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 1.50\n      ii_high_median: 0.015\n      median_difference: 1.48\n    result_rationale: \"S020 importance gradient present but moderate. Worst tier: 'At s020, the effect size (median_diff=1.48) is smaller and the practical significance unclear. Combined with GPQA showing no meaningful gradient at this level, s020 may be below the threshold where phase stratification matters—limiting the practical applicability of phase-gated approaches to only extreme compression regimes that nobody deploys'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"If GPQA fails at this level, practical relevance is limited to extreme sparsity.\"\n\n  - name: \"c3_bf16_ds_rand_s020\"\n    plan_id: \"c3_bf16_ds_rand_s020\"\n    description: \"Random at s020 — NS baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_high_median: 0.292\n      ii_low_median: 0.276\n      median_difference: -0.016\n      verdict: \"FAIL (flat)\"\n    result_rationale: \"DS random flat at s020. Same architecture-dependence argument as above. On LLaMA at s020, random d_z=0.373 (CI: 0.087-0.734) — significantly non-zero. So 'random flat at low sparsity' is a DeepSeek/Qwen property, not universal.\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Random flatness non-universal undermines strategy specificity narrative.\"\n\n  - name: \"c4_c4_entropy\"\n    plan_id: \"c4_c4_entropy\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek entropy/discrimination collapse mechanism\"\n    expected_results:\n      importance_entropy_delta_s030: -0.044\n      importance_gini_delta_s030: -0.081\n      random_entropy_delta_s030: +0.233\n    result_rationale: \"DeepSeek 机制数据 internally consistent。Worst tier 攻击：'The mechanism story works for one model but fails on Qwen (entropy reversal at s025). A mechanism that only explains one model's behavior is not a mechanism—it's a coincidence. Furthermore, discrimination collapse (Gini decrease) occurs for BOTH importance and random pruning (DS random Gini delta: -0.031 to -0.073), so it cannot explain why importance is DIFFERENT from random'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Mechanism non-universal (Qwen inconsistent) + Gini decrease in random undermines discriminative explanation.\"\n\n  - name: \"c4_qwen_c4_entropy\"\n    plan_id: \"c4_qwen_c4_entropy\"\n    description: \"Qwen entropy — expected negative/inconsistent\"\n    expected_results:\n      importance_entropy_delta_s025: +0.045\n      importance_entropy_delta_s030: -0.007\n      conclusion: \"negative — inconsistent with DeepSeek\"\n    result_rationale: \"Qwen s025 entropy 反转(+0.045) 直接否定 'entropy collapse as universal mechanism'。Worst tier 最大化利用：'The proposed discrimination collapse mechanism is refuted by your own cross-model data. If the mechanism doesn't generalize, the entire explanatory framework is model-specific rather than a fundamental insight about compound sparsity'。将 C4 从 'partially confirmed' 降级为 'speculative'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Mechanism claim severely weakened; need to downgrade to 'observed pattern on one model' rather than explanatory mechanism.\"\n\n  - name: \"c5_bf16_qw_imp_s030\"\n    plan_id: \"c5_bf16_qw_imp_s030\"\n    description: \"Qwen s030 cross-model replication\"\n    expected_results:\n      median_difference: 2.62\n      cohens_d: 1.44\n    result_rationale: \"Qwen replication 成功但 worst tier 重新框定：'Both models use Qwen2ForCausalLM architecture. This is a same-architecture replication (training-variant test), not a cross-architecture generalization. When you DO test cross-architecture (LLaMA), the strategy×phase interaction collapses. So you have strong within-architecture consistency but poor cross-architecture generalization—the opposite of what's needed for a general finding'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Same-architecture replication ≠ generalization. LLaMA failure is the real test.\"\n\n  - name: \"c5_c2_n500_deepseek\"\n    plan_id: \"c5_c2_n500_deepseek\"\n    description: \"DS n=500 high-power validation\"\n    expected_results:\n      imp_s030_median_ii: 8.48\n      imp_rand_ratio_range: \"15.5-38.6×\"\n      dose_response_monotonic: true\n      all_bonferroni_significant: true\n    result_rationale: \"N=500 gives overwhelming statistical power on DeepSeek MATH-500. Worst tier 不质疑统计显著性——质疑的是 external validity：'High power on one model + one benchmark doesn't compensate for failure to generalize. You've measured the same effect very precisely, but precision ≠ generalizability. The 15-38× ratio on MATH-500 shrinks to 2.3-3.8× on GSM8K and potentially ~1× on GPQA. This is textbook overfitting to a specific task'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Precision mistaken for generalizability. Task-dependence decay dominates.\"\n\n  - name: \"c5_c2_qw_n500_r3\"\n    plan_id: \"c5_c2_qw_n500_r3\"\n    description: \"QW n=500 high-power validation\"\n    expected_results:\n      imp_s030_median_ii: 3.155\n      imp_rand_ratio_range: \"2.7-20.1×\"\n      dose_response_monotonic: true\n    result_rationale: \"Qwen n=500 已经显示 ratio 比 DeepSeek 窄得多(2.7-20.1× vs 15.5-38.6×)。Worst tier: 'The ratio is already model-dependent (4-fold variation between DeepSeek and Qwen), benchmark-dependent (MATH-500 vs GSM8K further 5× shrinkage), and architecture-dependent (LLaMA ≈ 1×). You have a finding that varies 50-fold depending on context—that's not a robust phenomenon, that's a context-specific observation'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"50-fold context variation (1× to 38×) → not a robust universal finding.\"\n\n  - name: \"c5b_c5b_pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"c5b_c5b_pilot\"\n    description: \"Phase-aware mitigation pilot\"\n    expected_results:\n      oracle_recovery_pct: 18\n      gate_result: \"FAIL\"\n      heuristic_recovery_ci_crosses_zero: true\n    result_rationale: \"Mitigation 失败是 worst tier 最强武器：'You claim to discover a practically important phase×strategy interaction, but your own mitigation attempt (the direct practical implication) fails the pre-registered gate. Oracle recovery 18% < 30% threshold with CI crossing zero means even PERFECT phase knowledge doesn't help much. This fundamentally undermines the \"practical deployment teams need phase-stratified audit\" framing—if knowing the phase doesn't help you fix the problem, why does it matter that severity is phase-modulated?'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Failed mitigation is devastating for practical relevance claim. Reviewer: 'interesting observation, but so what?'\"\n\n  - name: \"c6_bf16_importance_s015\"\n    plan_id: \"c6_bf16_importance_s015\"\n    description: \"Dose-response starting point s015\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 0.398\n      sign_reversal: true\n      high_phase_mean_negative: true\n    result_rationale: \"S015 有 sign reversal（high phase mean 为负），worst tier 放大：'At s015, the high-phase II mean is negative (-0.15), meaning compound interaction is PROTECTIVE in early phases at low sparsity. This complicates the monotonic narrative—the interaction is not simply \"amplified in low-sparsity phase\" but shows a complex, non-monotonic pattern at the per-phase level. Your dose-response story cherry-picks the low-phase trajectory while ignoring sign reversals elsewhere'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Sign reversal at s015 high-phase complicates clean dose-response narrative.\"\n\n  - name: \"c6_bf16_importance_s020\"\n    plan_id: \"c6_bf16_importance_s020\"\n    description: \"Dose-response s020 point\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 1.496\n      median_difference: 1.48\n    result_rationale: \"S020 点 consistent with dose-response, but worst tier notes the 'growth rate' narrative: 0.40→1.50→7.20→14.64 是 sub-exponential。Reviewer: 'The dose-response is simply that more compression causes more degradation—this is trivially expected and not a contribution. Calling it \"sub-exponential\" doesn't add insight because we have no theoretical prediction for what the growth rate should be'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Dose-response is trivially expected; sub-exponential characterization adds minimal insight.\"\n\n  - name: \"c6_bf16_importance_s025\"\n    plan_id: \"c6_bf16_importance_s025\"\n    description: \"Dose-response s025 point\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 7.196\n    result_rationale: \"同上 dose-response 框架。在 worst tier 下整个 C6 claim 被视为 'stating the obvious'：更多 compression → 更多 degradation，以 phase-stratified 方式呈现但核心 insight 不超越 'severity increases with compression level'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Contributes to dose-response completeness but adds minimal novelty in worst tier.\"\n\n  - name: \"c6_bf16_importance_s030\"\n    plan_id: \"c6_bf16_importance_s030\"\n    description: \"Dose-response s030 endpoint\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 14.64\n      growth_factors: \"3.8×→4.8×→2.0× (decreasing)\"\n    result_rationale: \"Growth factor 递减(sub-exponential) 在 worst tier 被解读为 saturation：'The diminishing growth rate simply reflects ceiling effects—at 30% pruning, the model is already severely degraded (accuracy 4-10%), so there's less \"room\" for further phase-dependent degradation. This is a measurement artifact, not a meaningful characterization of compound interaction dynamics'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Sub-exponential growth reinterpreted as trivial ceiling effect.\"\n\n  - name: \"c7_c2_n500_deepseek\"\n    plan_id: \"c7_c2_n500_deepseek\"\n    description: \"N=500 statistical power confirmation\"\n    expected_results:\n      all_4_sparsities_bonferroni_significant: true\n      spearman_rho: 1.0\n    result_rationale: \"Statistical significance at n=500 是 trivially achieved for any non-zero effect with sufficient power。Worst tier: 'p-values at 10^-70 tell us the effect is non-zero—which was never in dispute. The question is whether it's MEANINGFULLY non-zero in a generalizable way. High precision on MATH-500 with DeepSeek is answering the wrong question if the effect doesn't replicate on GPQA or with different architectures'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Statistical significance ≠ practical or scientific significance. Wrong question answered precisely.\"\n\n  - name: \"c7_c2_qw_n500_r3\"\n    plan_id: \"c7_c2_qw_n500_r3\"\n    description: \"QW n=500 confirming dose-response\"\n    expected_results:\n      all_4_bonferroni_significant: true\n      mid_null_rate: 0.452\n    result_rationale: \"45.2% mid-null rate 在 worst tier 被放大：'Nearly half of Qwen problems produce null mid-phase measurements, meaning your three-phase framework doesn't apply to a large fraction of data. This high null rate suggests the phase segmentation is fragile and model-dependent—further evidence that the framework doesn't generalize'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"High mid-null rate questions phase framework applicability.\"\n\n  - name: \"c8_c3_llama\"\n    plan_id: \"c8_c3_llama\"\n    description: \"LLaMA cross-architecture validation n=50\"\n    expected_results:\n      imp_vs_rand_dz_s030: 0.335\n      significant_bonferroni_s030_only: true\n      random_phase_gradient_dz: \"0.35-0.44 (all significant)\"\n    result_rationale: \"LLaMA n=50 是 worst tier 的核心证据源。imp_vs_rand d_z 0.19-0.34(仅 s030 Bonferroni 显著) 已经很弱，但更致命的是 random 也有显著 phase gradient (d_z 0.35-0.44, CI 排除零)。Worst tier 解读：'On LLaMA, random masking shows phase gradient COMPARABLE to the importance-vs-random difference (random gradient d_z≈0.4 vs imp_vs_rand d_z≈0.3). This means phase gradient is a universal property of compression (not strategy-specific), and the small additional gradient from importance is within noise for 3 of 4 sparsity levels. The n=50 result that appeared \"partially confirming\" is likely noise amplification—n=250 will clarify'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: [\"Forest plot showing LLaMA imp_vs_rand CIs all crossing or barely excluding zero\"]\n    analysis: \"LLaMA data is the primary evidence FOR worst tier. Random gradient on LLaMA invalidates strategy specificity as universal.\"\n\n  - name: \"c10_gsm8k_profiling_ds\"\n    plan_id: \"c10_gsm8k_profiling_ds\"\n    description: \"DS GSM8K cross-benchmark importance gradient\"\n    expected_results:\n      imp_gradient_monotonic: true\n      imp_rand_ratio: \"2.3-3.8×\"\n      ratio_vs_math500: \"衰减 5-10×\"\n    result_rationale: \"GSM8K imp/rand ratio 从 MATH-500 15-36× 衰减至 2.3-3.8×。Worst tier 最大化利用这个衰减：'The defining feature of your paper—strategy specificity (15-36× ratio)—is benchmark-specific. On an easier benchmark (GSM8K), the ratio drops to 2.3-3.8×. Extrapolating the decay trend: MATH-500 (hard, long CoT) → GSM8K (medium, shorter CoT) → GPQA (hard but different domain) predicts ratio approaching 1.0 on GPQA. This is classic overfitting—the large effect exists only on the benchmark you optimized your analysis for'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: [\"Decay curve: MATH-500 ratio → GSM8K ratio → projected GPQA ratio ≈ 1\"]\n    analysis: \"5-10× decay from MATH-500 to GSM8K projects to near-null on GPQA. Task-specificity narrative.\"\n\n  - name: \"c10_gsm8k_profiling_qw\"\n    plan_id: \"c10_gsm8k_profiling_qw\"\n    description: \"QW GSM8K cross-benchmark gradient\"\n    expected_results:\n      imp_gradient_monotonic: true\n      s030_median_gradient: 2.092\n      qw_rand_s030: \"INVALID (technical failure)\"\n    result_rationale: \"QW random s030 INVALID 在 worst tier 是 missing data problem：'You cannot claim strategy specificity on GSM8K for Qwen because the random comparison is technically invalid. The 2.3-3.8× ratio comes only from DeepSeek. For Qwen, you have importance gradient but no clean random baseline—the claim is incomplete'。Partial data = partial conclusion。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Missing QW random baseline weakens GSM8K strategy specificity claim for Qwen.\"\n\n  - name: \"c10_gsm8k_qw_rand_s025_v2\"\n    plan_id: \"c10_gsm8k_qw_rand_s025_v2\"\n    description: \"QW random s025 on GSM8K\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_high_median: 0.72\n      ii_low_median: 1.46\n      verdict: \"PASS (random also has gradient)\"\n    result_rationale: \"关键：QW random s025 在 GSM8K 上也显示 phase gradient（low/high ratio = 2.0×）。这意味着在 GSM8K 上 random 也有 non-trivial phase gradient，进一步缩小 imp/rand 差异。Worst tier：'On GSM8K, even random masking shows 2× phase gradient for Qwen at s025. With importance showing ~2.9× (1.1/0.39 from profiling), the imp/rand ratio is barely above 1.5. Strategy specificity has essentially vanished on this benchmark for Qwen'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Random also shows gradient on GSM8K → imp/rand ratio approaches 1.5 for Qwen.\"\n\n  - name: \"c10_gsm8k_qw_rand_s030_v2\"\n    plan_id: \"c10_gsm8k_qw_rand_s030_v2\"\n    description: \"QW random s030 on GSM8K\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_high_median: 2.31\n      ii_low_median: 5.20\n      low_high_ratio: 2.25\n    result_rationale: \"QW random s030 GSM8K: low/high = 5.20/2.31 = 2.25×. Importance gradient at s030 = 2.092 (from profiling). Worst tier 计算：importance gradient 2.09 vs random gradient (5.20-2.31)=2.89 → random gradient LARGER than importance。'On GSM8K at s030, Qwen random masking produces a LARGER phase gradient than importance masking. This completely inverts the MATH-500 finding and confirms that strategy specificity is benchmark-specific. On GSM8K, random is not \"flat\"—it's arguably more phase-sensitive than importance'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: [\"Side-by-side: MATH-500 (importance >> random) vs GSM8K (random ≥ importance) for Qwen\"]\n    analysis: \"Inversion on GSM8K (random gradient ≥ importance) is devastating for strategy specificity universality.\"\n\n  - name: \"s3_c_bf16_ds_imp_s010\"\n    plan_id: \"s3_c_bf16_ds_imp_s010\"\n    description: \"DS s010 below onset threshold\"\n    expected_results:\n      verdict: \"FAIL\"\n      ii_low_median: 0.015\n      near_zero: true\n    result_rationale: \"S010 below threshold — expected and not controversial. Worst tier simply notes：'The onset threshold (~s015 for DeepSeek) is model-dependent and benchmark-dependent. If the effect only emerges above s015-s020 (15-20% pruning), the practical relevance is limited—few deployment scenarios use such extreme compound pruning'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Threshold characterization useful but limits practical scope.\"\n\n  - name: \"s3_c_bf16_qw_imp_s010\"\n    plan_id: \"s3_c_bf16_qw_imp_s010\"\n    description: \"QW s010 — onset characterization\"\n    expected_results:\n      overall_verdict: \"PASS (ci_overlap_test)\"\n      ii_low_median: -0.044\n      negative_values: true\n    result_rationale: \"QW s010 low-phase II median 为负(-0.044)，表面通过 CI overlap test 但实际 II 值 trivially small 且负。Worst tier：'Qwen at s010 shows NEGATIVE II in low-phase—compound interaction is slightly protective. This means the \"amplification in low-sparsity phase\" narrative has a sign reversal at low compression. The phenomenon is not monotonic across the full sparsity range'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Negative II at s010 complicates the monotonic amplification story.\"\n\n  - name: \"s3_c_bf16_qw_imp_s015\"\n    plan_id: \"s3_c_bf16_qw_imp_s015\"\n    description: \"QW s015 — at onset boundary\"\n    expected_results:\n      median_difference: 0.048\n      cohens_d: 0.37\n      bootstrap_ci_includes_zero: true\n    result_rationale: \"QW s015 CI 含零([-0.005, 0.110])，Cohen's d=0.37 (small)。Worst tier 关键点：'Qwen at s015 is borderline—CI includes zero, effect is small (d=0.37). This means the onset threshold for Qwen is s020, not s015 like DeepSeek. Model-dependent onset + benchmark-dependent magnitude + architecture-dependent strategy specificity = too many degrees of freedom for a general claim'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Borderline significance strengthens 'model-dependent, not universal' narrative.\"\n\n  - name: \"s7_c_c2_n500_deepseek\"\n    plan_id: \"s7_c_c2_n500_deepseek\"\n    description: \"DS n=500 monotonicity confirmation\"\n    expected_results:\n      spearman_rho: 1.0\n      dose_response_monotonic: true\n      perm_p: 0.042\n    result_rationale: \"Monotonicity 在 DeepSeek MATH-500 上 trivially expected with n=500 power. Worst tier notes permutation p=0.042 is barely significant（4 points，最小可能 p=1/24=0.042）——这不是 overwhelmingly significant 而是 mathematically the minimum possible p-value for 4 ordered points。'Your Spearman test with 4 dose levels has minimum possible p=0.042—achieving it doesn't prove monotonicity, it merely doesn't reject it. With only 4 points, any positively-trending dose-response will achieve rho=1.0'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Spearman rho=1.0 with 4 points is trivial; p=0.042 is minimum possible, not impressive.\"\n\n  - name: \"s7_c_c2_qw_n500_r3\"\n    plan_id: \"s7_c_c2_qw_n500_r3\"\n    description: \"QW n=500 monotonicity\"\n    expected_results:\n      spearman_rho: 1.0\n      perm_p: 0.042\n    result_rationale: \"同 DS。4 points rho=1.0 是 trivial。Worst tier：'Both models show monotonic dose-response, which is trivially expected (more compression = more degradation). This is not a finding—it's a sanity check. The actual contribution claim (strategy × phase interaction) needs separate validation which fails on LLaMA/GPQA'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Monotonicity is expected, not a contribution. Real test is interaction specificity.\"\n\n  - name: \"s7_c_bf16_qw_imp_s035\"\n    plan_id: \"s7_c_bf16_qw_imp_s035\"\n    description: \"QW s035 extending dose-response range\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 8.24\n      extends_monotonicity: true\n    result_rationale: \"S035 extends the curve but at 35% head pruning the model is nearly destroyed (ppl_low_both=58.0)。Worst tier：'Extending to 35% pruning where perplexity reaches 58× demonstrates the effect at a regime nobody deploys. This doesn't add practical relevance—it shows you can make the number bigger by breaking the model more'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Extreme sparsity extension adds no practical value; model essentially broken.\"\n\n  # --- RUNNING/QUEUED experiments: key predictions ---\n\n  - name: \"c8_llama_n250_fixed\"\n    plan_id: \"c8_llama_n250_fixed (registry: RUNNING)\"\n    description: \"LLaMA n=250 scaled cross-architecture validation — THE critical worst-tier experiment\"\n    expected_results:\n      imp_vs_rand_dz_s015: 0.11\n      imp_vs_rand_dz_s020: 0.14\n      imp_vs_rand_dz_s025: 0.17\n      imp_vs_rand_dz_s030: 0.19\n      bonferroni_significant_conditions: 0\n      phase_gradient_importance_dz_all: \">1.0 (robust)\"\n      phase_gradient_random_dz_all: \"0.30-0.45 (significant, CI excludes zero)\"\n      imp_vs_rand_monotonic: true\n      median_diff_s030: 0.18\n      median_diff_s030_ci: [-0.02, 0.38]\n    result_rationale: \"N=250 reveals that n=50 LLaMA result (d_z 0.34 at s030, Bonferroni p=0.029) was noise inflated. With 5× more data, the true d_z shrinks to ~0.19 — still positive (monotonic trend preserved) but entirely NS after Bonferroni correction (all 4 conditions p>0.05). Critically, within-importance phase gradient remains large (d_z>1.0) confirming phase modulation is robust, but imp_vs_rand d_z < 0.20 means strategy specificity is negligible on LLaMA architecture. Meanwhile, random phase gradient at d_z 0.30-0.45 with n=250 CI firmly excluding zero means random is ALSO phase-modulated on LLaMA. Interpretation: phase gradient is a universal compression phenomenon, not strategy-specific. The n=50 apparent significance was a false positive at the edge of the Bonferroni threshold.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: LLaMA n=250 imp_vs_rand d_z by sparsity, all NS (p>0.10 Bonferroni)\"\n      - \"Table: LLaMA random phase gradient d_z 0.30-0.45, all significant at n=250\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: LLaMA n=250 imp_vs_rand d_z with CI all crossing zero (or barely above)\"\n      - \"Comparison: DeepSeek imp_vs_rand d_z 0.44-0.80 vs LLaMA 0.11-0.19 — order of magnitude difference\"\n    analysis: \"This is the definitive worst-tier result. Strategy×phase interaction is architecture-specific: strong on Qwen2 (DeepSeek+Qwen), negligible on Llama. Core C1 framing ('strategy specificity is emergent') collapses to 'strategy specificity is an architecture-contingent phenomenon observed on Qwen2'. Paper must reframe: phase gradient is the universal finding, strategy modulation is one manifestation. Methodology contribution (II metric + phase-stratified analysis protocol) becomes the primary novelty.\"\n\n  - name: \"gpqa_ds_importance_s015\"\n    plan_id: \"gpqa_ds_importance_s015 (registry: RUNNING)\"\n    description: \"GPQA DeepSeek importance s015 — cross-benchmark hardest test\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 0.25\n      ii_high_median: 0.18\n      median_difference: 0.07\n      phase_gradient_monotonic: false\n      wilcoxon_p: 0.35\n      cohens_dz: 0.12\n      n_valid_problems: 35\n      mid_null_rate: 0.55\n    result_rationale: \"GPQA 是 hard science reasoning（physics/chemistry/biology），CoT 结构与 MATH-500 不同——更短、更 factual-retrieval oriented、less sequential computation。At s015 (lowest sparsity), compound interaction is expected to be weak even on MATH-500 (DS median_diff=0.39). On GPQA: (1) shorter CoT means less temporal structure → phase segmentation less meaningful (55% mid-null rate); (2) reasoning structure different from math → phase boundaries poorly align with actual cognitive demands; (3) at s015 the compression is too mild to trigger meaningful compound interaction on a different task type. Result: near-zero gradient, NS, non-monotonic because the signal is in the noise floor. The II values for high and low phases are within noise of each other because GPQA problems don't have the same 'exploration→computation→verification' phase structure that MATH-500 problems have.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: GPQA phase gradient vs MATH-500 at s015: DS MATH-500 median_diff=0.39 vs GPQA=0.07\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: GPQA phases showing flat/non-monotonic II pattern with overlapping CIs\"\n    analysis: \"GPQA s015 NS and non-monotonic. If s020 also fails, the cross-benchmark generalization story collapses: effect is MATH-500 specific (and partially GSM8K), not a general property of reasoning tasks.\"\n\n  - name: \"gpqa_ds_importance_s020\"\n    plan_id: \"gpqa_ds_importance_s020 (registry: QUEUED)\"\n    description: \"GPQA DeepSeek importance s020 — critical for decay trend\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 0.55\n      ii_high_median: 0.35\n      median_difference: 0.20\n      phase_gradient_monotonic: false\n      wilcoxon_p: 0.12\n      cohens_dz: 0.22\n      imp_rand_ratio_estimated: 1.3\n      n_valid_problems: 38\n      mid_null_rate: 0.50\n    result_rationale: \"S020 on GPQA: slightly larger effect than s015 (expected from dose-response) but still NS and weak. Key metric for worst tier: imp/rand ratio. If GPQA random at s020 produces median_diff ≈ 0.15 (extrapolating from LLaMA random behavior where random also shows phase gradient), then imp/rand ratio = 0.20/0.15 ≈ 1.3 — within the [0.8, 1.8] worst tier range. This confirms the decay trend: MATH-500 ratio 15-36× → GSM8K 2.3-3.8× → GPQA ≈ 1.0-1.5×. The gradient IS there (positive median_diff) but it's (a) weak, (b) not significant, (c) not specific to importance strategy. The CoT structure in GPQA (shorter chains, more knowledge retrieval) doesn't create the pronounced phase differentiation that MATH-500's long exploratory reasoning chains do.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Cross-benchmark imp/rand ratio decay — MATH-500: 15-36× | GSM8K: 2.3-3.8× | GPQA: ~1.3×\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Decay plot: strategy specificity ratio as function of benchmark/task type\"\n      - \"GPQA phase distribution showing high mid-null rate and weak phase separation\"\n    analysis: \"GPQA s020 confirms the worst-tier prediction: strategy specificity vanishes on tasks with different CoT structure. The paper's core finding is MATH-500 specific (where long sequential reasoning creates pronounced phases). Reframe: 'Phase-dependent heterogeneity is most pronounced in tasks requiring extended sequential computation (MATH-500, partially GSM8K) and attenuates on tasks with shorter/different reasoning structures (GPQA). This task-dependence is itself an important finding for the methodology framework—it identifies WHEN phase-stratified analysis is most informative'.\"\n\n  # --- Reviewer simulation ---\n\n  - name: \"reviewer_assessment\"\n    plan_id: \"meta-analysis\"\n    description: \"Simulated reviewer scores and objections under worst tier\"\n    expected_results:\n      reviewer_1_score: 2.5\n      reviewer_1_main_concern: \"Novelty insufficient — Physics of KV Cache (Mar 2026) already establishes phase-dependent compression behavior. This paper adds data points but no new theoretical insight.\"\n      reviewer_2_score: 3.0\n      reviewer_2_main_concern: \"Generalizability — effect is architecture-specific (fails on LLaMA) and task-specific (vanishes on GPQA). Scope too narrow for EMNLP.\"\n      reviewer_3_score: 2.5\n      reviewer_3_main_concern: \"Practical impact — mitigation pilot failed. Without actionable downstream benefit, the observation is academically interesting but not a contribution.\"\n      average_score: 2.67\n      novelty_challenged: 3\n      accept_probability: 0.10\n    result_rationale: \"In worst tier, all three reviewers challenge novelty from different angles. R1 focuses on prior work overlap (Physics of KV Cache covers phase-dependent behavior theoretically, HIES covers discrimination collapse empirically). R2 focuses on generalizability failure (LLaMA n=250 NS, GPQA ≈1×). R3 focuses on 'so what' (mitigation failed, no practical protocol validated). The combination is fatal for acceptance as a 'finding paper'. The reframe to 'methodology paper' (II metric + phase-stratified audit protocol) partially addresses R3 but doesn't fully resolve R1 (what's novel about proposing a metric?) or R2 (if the method only works on one architecture/benchmark, what's the point?). Average 2.67 with all three challenging novelty → reject with encouragement to resubmit after broader validation.\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Reframe strategy: (1) Position as 'complementary to Physics of KV Cache' not competing; (2) Emphasize methodology over finding; (3) Acknowledge task/architecture dependence as boundary condition, frame it as the secondary contribution (identifying when phase analysis matters). Accept probability 5-20%.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56698,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56698},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a75bff4-afe9-4dc7-a729-1c3fa93fc9a2","uuid":"0a011f24-6bab-47d6-9bf5-ae5ec275dd7d"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":299880,"duration_api_ms":301430,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: \"Reframe 不降级目标（仍冲 EMNLP），但从 'finding paper' 转向 'methodology + diagnostic framework' contribution。核心 claim 从 'severity is strategy×phase emergent' 收缩为 'compound interaction exhibits phase-dependent heterogeneity that standard evaluation misses'。Phase gradient 作为 robust phenomenon 保留（importance 内部 d_z>1.0 跨所有模型始终成立），strategy specificity 降级为 'one manifestation that varies by context'。Practical hook：phase-stratified audit protocol + open-source toolkit。Related Work 定位为 complementary to Physics of KV Cache。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"c1_bf16_importance_s025\"\n    plan_id: \"c1_bf16_importance_s025\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek importance masking s025 phase gradient\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_high_median: 0.032\n      ii_mid_median: 1.12\n      ii_low_median: 7.20\n      median_difference: 7.16\n      gradient_direction: \"monotonic increasing\"\n    result_rationale: \"Importance 内部 phase gradient 在 worst tier 下依然成立——这是 robust phenomenon。问题不在 importance 本身的 gradient，而在于 random 也可能表现出类似 gradient（尤其在 LLaMA 架构上），导致 strategy specificity 被质疑。DeepSeek s025 importance 数据本身不受 worst tier 影响，因为 worst 的核心打击点是跨架构/跨 benchmark 的 strategy 区分度消失，不是 importance gradient 本身消失。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: [\"Phase gradient bar chart 仍显示 low>>mid>>high，但 reviewer 会注脚 'also observed in random on LLaMA'\"]\n    analysis: \"数据本身 PASS，但 worst tier 解读为 'phase gradient is universal phenomenon not specific to importance strategy'——需在论文中预防性承认这一解读可能性。\"\n\n  - name: \"c1_bf16_ds_rand_s025\"\n    plan_id: \"c1_bf16_ds_rand_s025\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek random masking s025 — flat gradient baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_high_median: 0.82\n      ii_mid_median: 0.93\n      ii_low_median: 1.36\n      median_difference: 0.54\n      pass_fail: \"FAIL (flat)\"\n    result_rationale: \"DeepSeek random 在 s025 确实 flat——但 worst tier 的攻击点是：(1) LLaMA random 不 flat（d_z 0.35-0.44），(2) GPQA 上 importance/random ratio 可能趋近 1.0。所以即使 DS random s025 flat，reviewer 可以论证这仅是 architecture-specific 而非 universal property of randomness。Random 在某些架构上也有 phase gradient → strategy specificity 不是 fundamental distinction 而是 contingent observation。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"FAIL verdict 表面支持 strategy specificity，但 LLaMA 数据否定了这一结论的普适性。\"\n\n  - name: \"c1_bf16_qw_imp_s025\"\n    plan_id: \"c1_bf16_qw_imp_s025\"\n    description: \"Qwen cross-model replication importance s025\"\n    expected_results:\n      median_difference: 1.11\n      cohens_d: 1.23\n      permutation_p: 0.0\n    result_rationale: \"Qwen importance gradient 在 worst tier 下同样 robust——两个 Qwen2 架构模型一致。但 reviewer 解读：'两个模型共享 Qwen2ForCausalLM 架构，不是独立验证。LLaMA 上效应弱化证明 architecture 是 confound'。Cross-model 变成 'same-architecture replication' 而非 'generalization evidence'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"数值强，但被框定为 architecture-specific phenomenon 的重复测量而非独立泛化。\"\n\n  - name: \"c1_sf5_asymmetric_spot\"\n    plan_id: \"c1_sf5_asymmetric_spot\"\n    description: \"Asymmetric head/KV configs\"\n    expected_results:\n      config_a_D: 19.13\n      config_b_D: 18.25\n      gradient_consistent: true\n    result_rationale: \"Asymmetric configs 仍显示 gradient——worst tier 不否认 DeepSeek 上 compound interaction 存在 phase modulation。攻击点转移至：'yes compound interaction is phase-modulated on DeepSeek Qwen2 architecture, but this is architecture-specific, not fundamental'。Ablation 变成 'thorough characterization of one architecture' 而非 'generalizable finding'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Passes criterion but scope-limited in worst tier framing.\"\n\n  - name: \"c1_c2_accuracy_eval\"\n    plan_id: \"c1_c2_accuracy_eval\"\n    description: \"Accuracy degradation across sparsity levels\"\n    expected_results:\n      ds_dense_acc: 0.52\n      ds_s030_acc: 0.10\n      ds_s030_delta: -0.42\n      qw_s030_acc: 0.14\n      qw_s030_delta: -0.18\n    result_rationale: \"Accuracy 大幅下降不被争议——compound sparsity 有 practical impact 是共识。Worst tier 攻击的不是 'compound sparsity hurts' 而是 'whether the phase×strategy interaction is the useful framing'。Reviewer: 'Everyone knows compound compression hurts. The question is whether your phase-stratified analysis adds actionable insight beyond what aggregate metrics already show—and your mitigation pilot failed'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Accuracy eval 本身不受 worst tier 影响，但 'so what' 质疑加强——因为 mitigation 未成功。\"\n\n  - name: \"c2_bf16_importance_s030\"\n    plan_id: \"c2_bf16_importance_s030\"\n    description: \"Phase gradient at highest sparsity\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 14.64\n      ii_high_median: 0.053\n      low_high_ratio: 276\n      median_difference: 14.59\n    result_rationale: \"S030 importance gradient 极强（276×），worst tier 不否认这个数字。但 reviewer 框架：'Large effect at extreme sparsity (30% heads pruned) is unsurprising—of course severe compression interacts with everything. The interesting question is whether this is strategy-specific, and your LLaMA data + GPQA data suggest it's not'。效应量大但 novelty 消失。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Strong numbers, weak novelty interpretation in worst tier.\"\n\n  - name: \"c2_v6_importance_s030\"\n    plan_id: \"c2_v6_importance_s030\"\n    description: \"v6 pipeline s030 results\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 34.69\n      ii_high_median: 0.88\n      bootstrap_gradient: 41.92\n    result_rationale: \"V6 pipeline 数字更大（不同 II 定义），但同样面临 'so what' 问题。Worst tier 下 reviewer 说 'these large numbers reflect your specific II metric definition, not necessarily a practically meaningful phase interaction. The metric itself is not validated against downstream task performance beyond the failed mitigation pilot'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Metric validity questioned without successful downstream application.\"\n\n  - name: \"c2_think_phase_validation\"\n    plan_id: \"c2_think_phase_validation\"\n    description: \"Phase segmentation alignment with think/answer\"\n    expected_results:\n      median_kappa: 0.887\n      thinking_in_low_sparsity: 0.578\n      answer_in_high_sparsity: 0.627\n    result_rationale: \"Phase segmentation 与 think/answer 对齐度中等（57.8%/62.7%），worst tier 解读：'Phase segmentation only partially aligns with semantic phases—42% of thinking tokens end up in high-sparsity phase. This imperfect alignment weakens the mechanistic story because the \"phases\" are statistical artifacts of sparsity distribution, not semantic constructs'。Kappa 0.887 看似高但是 adaptive threshold 产物。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Reviewer questions whether 'phases' have semantic meaning beyond statistical convenience.\"\n\n  - name: \"c2_acc_qw_s030_n100\"\n    plan_id: \"c2_acc_qw_s030_n100\"\n    description: \"Qwen s030 accuracy n=100\"\n    expected_results:\n      combined_acc: 0.19\n      batch_effect: \"batch1=14% vs batch2=24%\"\n    result_rationale: \"Batch effect (14% vs 24%) 在 worst tier 被放大：'10pp batch variation on n=50 suggests high measurement noise. Combined 19% vs dense 46% confirms degradation, but the variance raises questions about reproducibility of finer-grained phase-level measurements'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Batch variability undermines confidence in fine-grained per-phase claims.\"\n\n  - name: \"c2_acc_ds_s015_8k_v2\"\n    plan_id: \"c2_acc_ds_s015_8k_v2\"\n    description: \"DS s015 accuracy with 8k token limit\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.48\n      truncation_rate: 0.32\n      non_truncated_accuracy: 0.706\n    result_rationale: \"32% truncation rate 在 worst tier 是 confound：'16 of 50 problems were truncated at s015, which conflates compression-induced degradation with generation length limitation. Non-truncated accuracy (70.6%) suggests most degradation comes from truncation, not phase-dependent compound interaction'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Truncation confound weakens accuracy as supporting evidence for phase-dependent severity.\"\n\n  - name: \"c3_v6_importance_s025\"\n    plan_id: \"c3_v6_importance_s025\"\n    description: \"Crossover evidence — importance phase gradient\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 24.16\n      ii_high_median: 0.66\n      ratio: 36\n    result_rationale: \"Crossover claim 在 worst tier 被重新解读：'At s025, importance high_phase (0.032) < random (0.818) while importance low_phase (7.196) > random (1.363). But this \"crossover\" requires comparing importance vs random—if strategy specificity doesn't generalize (LLaMA, GPQA), the crossover is just an artifact of comparing two things that behave similarly on other architectures'。Crossover 依赖 strategy specificity 成立。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Crossover claim logically depends on strategy specificity; if specificity is architecture-specific, crossover is too.\"\n\n  - name: \"c3_v6_random_s025\"\n    plan_id: \"c3_v6_random_s025\"\n    description: \"Random flat at s025 — crossover baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 2.91\n      ii_high_median: 3.00\n      bootstrap_p: 0.559\n      verdict: \"FAIL (flat)\"\n    result_rationale: \"V6 random s025 flat (bootstrap_p=0.559) 在 DeepSeek 上支持 crossover。Worst tier 反驳：'Random is flat on DeepSeek at s025 but NOT on LLaMA (d_z 0.45 at s025, CI excludes zero). The flatness of random is architecture-dependent, so the crossover phenomenon is also architecture-dependent. On LLaMA, both strategies show phase gradient → no meaningful crossover'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Architecture-dependence of random behavior invalidates universality of crossover.\"\n\n  - name: \"c3_bf16_importance_s020\"\n    plan_id: \"c3_bf16_importance_s020\"\n    description: \"Importance at moderate sparsity\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 1.50\n      ii_high_median: 0.015\n      median_difference: 1.48\n    result_rationale: \"S020 importance gradient present but moderate. Worst tier: 'At s020, the effect size (median_diff=1.48) is smaller and the practical significance unclear. Combined with GPQA showing no meaningful gradient at this level, s020 may be below the threshold where phase stratification matters—limiting the practical applicability of phase-gated approaches to only extreme compression regimes that nobody deploys'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"If GPQA fails at this level, practical relevance is limited to extreme sparsity.\"\n\n  - name: \"c3_bf16_ds_rand_s020\"\n    plan_id: \"c3_bf16_ds_rand_s020\"\n    description: \"Random at s020 — NS baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_high_median: 0.292\n      ii_low_median: 0.276\n      median_difference: -0.016\n      verdict: \"FAIL (flat)\"\n    result_rationale: \"DS random flat at s020. Same architecture-dependence argument as above. On LLaMA at s020, random d_z=0.373 (CI: 0.087-0.734) — significantly non-zero. So 'random flat at low sparsity' is a DeepSeek/Qwen property, not universal.\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Random flatness non-universal undermines strategy specificity narrative.\"\n\n  - name: \"c4_c4_entropy\"\n    plan_id: \"c4_c4_entropy\"\n    description: \"DeepSeek entropy/discrimination collapse mechanism\"\n    expected_results:\n      importance_entropy_delta_s030: -0.044\n      importance_gini_delta_s030: -0.081\n      random_entropy_delta_s030: +0.233\n    result_rationale: \"DeepSeek 机制数据 internally consistent。Worst tier 攻击：'The mechanism story works for one model but fails on Qwen (entropy reversal at s025). A mechanism that only explains one model's behavior is not a mechanism—it's a coincidence. Furthermore, discrimination collapse (Gini decrease) occurs for BOTH importance and random pruning (DS random Gini delta: -0.031 to -0.073), so it cannot explain why importance is DIFFERENT from random'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Mechanism non-universal (Qwen inconsistent) + Gini decrease in random undermines discriminative explanation.\"\n\n  - name: \"c4_qwen_c4_entropy\"\n    plan_id: \"c4_qwen_c4_entropy\"\n    description: \"Qwen entropy — expected negative/inconsistent\"\n    expected_results:\n      importance_entropy_delta_s025: +0.045\n      importance_entropy_delta_s030: -0.007\n      conclusion: \"negative — inconsistent with DeepSeek\"\n    result_rationale: \"Qwen s025 entropy 反转(+0.045) 直接否定 'entropy collapse as universal mechanism'。Worst tier 最大化利用：'The proposed discrimination collapse mechanism is refuted by your own cross-model data. If the mechanism doesn't generalize, the entire explanatory framework is model-specific rather than a fundamental insight about compound sparsity'。将 C4 从 'partially confirmed' 降级为 'speculative'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Mechanism claim severely weakened; need to downgrade to 'observed pattern on one model' rather than explanatory mechanism.\"\n\n  - name: \"c5_bf16_qw_imp_s030\"\n    plan_id: \"c5_bf16_qw_imp_s030\"\n    description: \"Qwen s030 cross-model replication\"\n    expected_results:\n      median_difference: 2.62\n      cohens_d: 1.44\n    result_rationale: \"Qwen replication 成功但 worst tier 重新框定：'Both models use Qwen2ForCausalLM architecture. This is a same-architecture replication (training-variant test), not a cross-architecture generalization. When you DO test cross-architecture (LLaMA), the strategy×phase interaction collapses. So you have strong within-architecture consistency but poor cross-architecture generalization—the opposite of what's needed for a general finding'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Same-architecture replication ≠ generalization. LLaMA failure is the real test.\"\n\n  - name: \"c5_c2_n500_deepseek\"\n    plan_id: \"c5_c2_n500_deepseek\"\n    description: \"DS n=500 high-power validation\"\n    expected_results:\n      imp_s030_median_ii: 8.48\n      imp_rand_ratio_range: \"15.5-38.6×\"\n      dose_response_monotonic: true\n      all_bonferroni_significant: true\n    result_rationale: \"N=500 gives overwhelming statistical power on DeepSeek MATH-500. Worst tier 不质疑统计显著性——质疑的是 external validity：'High power on one model + one benchmark doesn't compensate for failure to generalize. You've measured the same effect very precisely, but precision ≠ generalizability. The 15-38× ratio on MATH-500 shrinks to 2.3-3.8× on GSM8K and potentially ~1× on GPQA. This is textbook overfitting to a specific task'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Precision mistaken for generalizability. Task-dependence decay dominates.\"\n\n  - name: \"c5_c2_qw_n500_r3\"\n    plan_id: \"c5_c2_qw_n500_r3\"\n    description: \"QW n=500 high-power validation\"\n    expected_results:\n      imp_s030_median_ii: 3.155\n      imp_rand_ratio_range: \"2.7-20.1×\"\n      dose_response_monotonic: true\n    result_rationale: \"Qwen n=500 已经显示 ratio 比 DeepSeek 窄得多(2.7-20.1× vs 15.5-38.6×)。Worst tier: 'The ratio is already model-dependent (4-fold variation between DeepSeek and Qwen), benchmark-dependent (MATH-500 vs GSM8K further 5× shrinkage), and architecture-dependent (LLaMA ≈ 1×). You have a finding that varies 50-fold depending on context—that's not a robust phenomenon, that's a context-specific observation'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"50-fold context variation (1× to 38×) → not a robust universal finding.\"\n\n  - name: \"c5b_c5b_pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"c5b_c5b_pilot\"\n    description: \"Phase-aware mitigation pilot\"\n    expected_results:\n      oracle_recovery_pct: 18\n      gate_result: \"FAIL\"\n      heuristic_recovery_ci_crosses_zero: true\n    result_rationale: \"Mitigation 失败是 worst tier 最强武器：'You claim to discover a practically important phase×strategy interaction, but your own mitigation attempt (the direct practical implication) fails the pre-registered gate. Oracle recovery 18% < 30% threshold with CI crossing zero means even PERFECT phase knowledge doesn't help much. This fundamentally undermines the \"practical deployment teams need phase-stratified audit\" framing—if knowing the phase doesn't help you fix the problem, why does it matter that severity is phase-modulated?'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Failed mitigation is devastating for practical relevance claim. Reviewer: 'interesting observation, but so what?'\"\n\n  - name: \"c6_bf16_importance_s015\"\n    plan_id: \"c6_bf16_importance_s015\"\n    description: \"Dose-response starting point s015\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 0.398\n      sign_reversal: true\n      high_phase_mean_negative: true\n    result_rationale: \"S015 有 sign reversal（high phase mean 为负），worst tier 放大：'At s015, the high-phase II mean is negative (-0.15), meaning compound interaction is PROTECTIVE in early phases at low sparsity. This complicates the monotonic narrative—the interaction is not simply \"amplified in low-sparsity phase\" but shows a complex, non-monotonic pattern at the per-phase level. Your dose-response story cherry-picks the low-phase trajectory while ignoring sign reversals elsewhere'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Sign reversal at s015 high-phase complicates clean dose-response narrative.\"\n\n  - name: \"c6_bf16_importance_s020\"\n    plan_id: \"c6_bf16_importance_s020\"\n    description: \"Dose-response s020 point\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 1.496\n      median_difference: 1.48\n    result_rationale: \"S020 点 consistent with dose-response, but worst tier notes the 'growth rate' narrative: 0.40→1.50→7.20→14.64 是 sub-exponential。Reviewer: 'The dose-response is simply that more compression causes more degradation—this is trivially expected and not a contribution. Calling it \"sub-exponential\" doesn't add insight because we have no theoretical prediction for what the growth rate should be'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Dose-response is trivially expected; sub-exponential characterization adds minimal insight.\"\n\n  - name: \"c6_bf16_importance_s025\"\n    plan_id: \"c6_bf16_importance_s025\"\n    description: \"Dose-response s025 point\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 7.196\n    result_rationale: \"同上 dose-response 框架。在 worst tier 下整个 C6 claim 被视为 'stating the obvious'：更多 compression → 更多 degradation，以 phase-stratified 方式呈现但核心 insight 不超越 'severity increases with compression level'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Contributes to dose-response completeness but adds minimal novelty in worst tier.\"\n\n  - name: \"c6_bf16_importance_s030\"\n    plan_id: \"c6_bf16_importance_s030\"\n    description: \"Dose-response s030 endpoint\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 14.64\n      growth_factors: \"3.8×→4.8×→2.0× (decreasing)\"\n    result_rationale: \"Growth factor 递减(sub-exponential) 在 worst tier 被解读为 saturation：'The diminishing growth rate simply reflects ceiling effects—at 30% pruning, the model is already severely degraded (accuracy 4-10%), so there's less \"room\" for further phase-dependent degradation. This is a measurement artifact, not a meaningful characterization of compound interaction dynamics'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Sub-exponential growth reinterpreted as trivial ceiling effect.\"\n\n  - name: \"c7_c2_n500_deepseek\"\n    plan_id: \"c7_c2_n500_deepseek\"\n    description: \"N=500 statistical power confirmation\"\n    expected_results:\n      all_4_sparsities_bonferroni_significant: true\n      spearman_rho: 1.0\n    result_rationale: \"Statistical significance at n=500 是 trivially achieved for any non-zero effect with sufficient power。Worst tier: 'p-values at 10^-70 tell us the effect is non-zero—which was never in dispute. The question is whether it's MEANINGFULLY non-zero in a generalizable way. High precision on MATH-500 with DeepSeek is answering the wrong question if the effect doesn't replicate on GPQA or with different architectures'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Statistical significance ≠ practical or scientific significance. Wrong question answered precisely.\"\n\n  - name: \"c7_c2_qw_n500_r3\"\n    plan_id: \"c7_c2_qw_n500_r3\"\n    description: \"QW n=500 confirming dose-response\"\n    expected_results:\n      all_4_bonferroni_significant: true\n      mid_null_rate: 0.452\n    result_rationale: \"45.2% mid-null rate 在 worst tier 被放大：'Nearly half of Qwen problems produce null mid-phase measurements, meaning your three-phase framework doesn't apply to a large fraction of data. This high null rate suggests the phase segmentation is fragile and model-dependent—further evidence that the framework doesn't generalize'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"High mid-null rate questions phase framework applicability.\"\n\n  - name: \"c8_c3_llama\"\n    plan_id: \"c8_c3_llama\"\n    description: \"LLaMA cross-architecture validation n=50\"\n    expected_results:\n      imp_vs_rand_dz_s030: 0.335\n      significant_bonferroni_s030_only: true\n      random_phase_gradient_dz: \"0.35-0.44 (all significant)\"\n    result_rationale: \"LLaMA n=50 是 worst tier 的核心证据源。imp_vs_rand d_z 0.19-0.34(仅 s030 Bonferroni 显著) 已经很弱，但更致命的是 random 也有显著 phase gradient (d_z 0.35-0.44, CI 排除零)。Worst tier 解读：'On LLaMA, random masking shows phase gradient COMPARABLE to the importance-vs-random difference (random gradient d_z≈0.4 vs imp_vs_rand d_z≈0.3). This means phase gradient is a universal property of compression (not strategy-specific), and the small additional gradient from importance is within noise for 3 of 4 sparsity levels. The n=50 result that appeared \"partially confirming\" is likely noise amplification—n=250 will clarify'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: [\"Forest plot showing LLaMA imp_vs_rand CIs all crossing or barely excluding zero\"]\n    analysis: \"LLaMA data is the primary evidence FOR worst tier. Random gradient on LLaMA invalidates strategy specificity as universal.\"\n\n  - name: \"c10_gsm8k_profiling_ds\"\n    plan_id: \"c10_gsm8k_profiling_ds\"\n    description: \"DS GSM8K cross-benchmark importance gradient\"\n    expected_results:\n      imp_gradient_monotonic: true\n      imp_rand_ratio: \"2.3-3.8×\"\n      ratio_vs_math500: \"衰减 5-10×\"\n    result_rationale: \"GSM8K imp/rand ratio 从 MATH-500 15-36× 衰减至 2.3-3.8×。Worst tier 最大化利用这个衰减：'The defining feature of your paper—strategy specificity (15-36× ratio)—is benchmark-specific. On an easier benchmark (GSM8K), the ratio drops to 2.3-3.8×. Extrapolating the decay trend: MATH-500 (hard, long CoT) → GSM8K (medium, shorter CoT) → GPQA (hard but different domain) predicts ratio approaching 1.0 on GPQA. This is classic overfitting—the large effect exists only on the benchmark you optimized your analysis for'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: [\"Decay curve: MATH-500 ratio → GSM8K ratio → projected GPQA ratio ≈ 1\"]\n    analysis: \"5-10× decay from MATH-500 to GSM8K projects to near-null on GPQA. Task-specificity narrative.\"\n\n  - name: \"c10_gsm8k_profiling_qw\"\n    plan_id: \"c10_gsm8k_profiling_qw\"\n    description: \"QW GSM8K cross-benchmark gradient\"\n    expected_results:\n      imp_gradient_monotonic: true\n      s030_median_gradient: 2.092\n      qw_rand_s030: \"INVALID (technical failure)\"\n    result_rationale: \"QW random s030 INVALID 在 worst tier 是 missing data problem：'You cannot claim strategy specificity on GSM8K for Qwen because the random comparison is technically invalid. The 2.3-3.8× ratio comes only from DeepSeek. For Qwen, you have importance gradient but no clean random baseline—the claim is incomplete'。Partial data = partial conclusion。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Missing QW random baseline weakens GSM8K strategy specificity claim for Qwen.\"\n\n  - name: \"c10_gsm8k_qw_rand_s025_v2\"\n    plan_id: \"c10_gsm8k_qw_rand_s025_v2\"\n    description: \"QW random s025 on GSM8K\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_high_median: 0.72\n      ii_low_median: 1.46\n      verdict: \"PASS (random also has gradient)\"\n    result_rationale: \"关键：QW random s025 在 GSM8K 上也显示 phase gradient（low/high ratio = 2.0×）。这意味着在 GSM8K 上 random 也有 non-trivial phase gradient，进一步缩小 imp/rand 差异。Worst tier：'On GSM8K, even random masking shows 2× phase gradient for Qwen at s025. With importance showing ~2.9× (1.1/0.39 from profiling), the imp/rand ratio is barely above 1.5. Strategy specificity has essentially vanished on this benchmark for Qwen'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Random also shows gradient on GSM8K → imp/rand ratio approaches 1.5 for Qwen.\"\n\n  - name: \"c10_gsm8k_qw_rand_s030_v2\"\n    plan_id: \"c10_gsm8k_qw_rand_s030_v2\"\n    description: \"QW random s030 on GSM8K\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_high_median: 2.31\n      ii_low_median: 5.20\n      low_high_ratio: 2.25\n    result_rationale: \"QW random s030 GSM8K: low/high = 5.20/2.31 = 2.25×. Importance gradient at s030 = 2.092 (from profiling). Worst tier 计算：importance gradient 2.09 vs random gradient (5.20-2.31)=2.89 → random gradient LARGER than importance。'On GSM8K at s030, Qwen random masking produces a LARGER phase gradient than importance masking. This completely inverts the MATH-500 finding and confirms that strategy specificity is benchmark-specific. On GSM8K, random is not \"flat\"—it's arguably more phase-sensitive than importance'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: [\"Side-by-side: MATH-500 (importance >> random) vs GSM8K (random ≥ importance) for Qwen\"]\n    analysis: \"Inversion on GSM8K (random gradient ≥ importance) is devastating for strategy specificity universality.\"\n\n  - name: \"s3_c_bf16_ds_imp_s010\"\n    plan_id: \"s3_c_bf16_ds_imp_s010\"\n    description: \"DS s010 below onset threshold\"\n    expected_results:\n      verdict: \"FAIL\"\n      ii_low_median: 0.015\n      near_zero: true\n    result_rationale: \"S010 below threshold — expected and not controversial. Worst tier simply notes：'The onset threshold (~s015 for DeepSeek) is model-dependent and benchmark-dependent. If the effect only emerges above s015-s020 (15-20% pruning), the practical relevance is limited—few deployment scenarios use such extreme compound pruning'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Threshold characterization useful but limits practical scope.\"\n\n  - name: \"s3_c_bf16_qw_imp_s010\"\n    plan_id: \"s3_c_bf16_qw_imp_s010\"\n    description: \"QW s010 — onset characterization\"\n    expected_results:\n      overall_verdict: \"PASS (ci_overlap_test)\"\n      ii_low_median: -0.044\n      negative_values: true\n    result_rationale: \"QW s010 low-phase II median 为负(-0.044)，表面通过 CI overlap test 但实际 II 值 trivially small 且负。Worst tier：'Qwen at s010 shows NEGATIVE II in low-phase—compound interaction is slightly protective. This means the \"amplification in low-sparsity phase\" narrative has a sign reversal at low compression. The phenomenon is not monotonic across the full sparsity range'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Negative II at s010 complicates the monotonic amplification story.\"\n\n  - name: \"s3_c_bf16_qw_imp_s015\"\n    plan_id: \"s3_c_bf16_qw_imp_s015\"\n    description: \"QW s015 — at onset boundary\"\n    expected_results:\n      median_difference: 0.048\n      cohens_d: 0.37\n      bootstrap_ci_includes_zero: true\n    result_rationale: \"QW s015 CI 含零([-0.005, 0.110])，Cohen's d=0.37 (small)。Worst tier 关键点：'Qwen at s015 is borderline—CI includes zero, effect is small (d=0.37). This means the onset threshold for Qwen is s020, not s015 like DeepSeek. Model-dependent onset + benchmark-dependent magnitude + architecture-dependent strategy specificity = too many degrees of freedom for a general claim'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Borderline significance strengthens 'model-dependent, not universal' narrative.\"\n\n  - name: \"s7_c_c2_n500_deepseek\"\n    plan_id: \"s7_c_c2_n500_deepseek\"\n    description: \"DS n=500 monotonicity confirmation\"\n    expected_results:\n      spearman_rho: 1.0\n      dose_response_monotonic: true\n      perm_p: 0.042\n    result_rationale: \"Monotonicity 在 DeepSeek MATH-500 上 trivially expected with n=500 power. Worst tier notes permutation p=0.042 is barely significant（4 points，最小可能 p=1/24=0.042）——这不是 overwhelmingly significant 而是 mathematically the minimum possible p-value for 4 ordered points。'Your Spearman test with 4 dose levels has minimum possible p=0.042—achieving it doesn't prove monotonicity, it merely doesn't reject it. With only 4 points, any positively-trending dose-response will achieve rho=1.0'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Spearman rho=1.0 with 4 points is trivial; p=0.042 is minimum possible, not impressive.\"\n\n  - name: \"s7_c_c2_qw_n500_r3\"\n    plan_id: \"s7_c_c2_qw_n500_r3\"\n    description: \"QW n=500 monotonicity\"\n    expected_results:\n      spearman_rho: 1.0\n      perm_p: 0.042\n    result_rationale: \"同 DS。4 points rho=1.0 是 trivial。Worst tier：'Both models show monotonic dose-response, which is trivially expected (more compression = more degradation). This is not a finding—it's a sanity check. The actual contribution claim (strategy × phase interaction) needs separate validation which fails on LLaMA/GPQA'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Monotonicity is expected, not a contribution. Real test is interaction specificity.\"\n\n  - name: \"s7_c_bf16_qw_imp_s035\"\n    plan_id: \"s7_c_bf16_qw_imp_s035\"\n    description: \"QW s035 extending dose-response range\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 8.24\n      extends_monotonicity: true\n    result_rationale: \"S035 extends the curve but at 35% head pruning the model is nearly destroyed (ppl_low_both=58.0)。Worst tier：'Extending to 35% pruning where perplexity reaches 58× demonstrates the effect at a regime nobody deploys. This doesn't add practical relevance—it shows you can make the number bigger by breaking the model more'。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Extreme sparsity extension adds no practical value; model essentially broken.\"\n\n  # --- RUNNING/QUEUED experiments: key predictions ---\n\n  - name: \"c8_llama_n250_fixed\"\n    plan_id: \"c8_llama_n250_fixed (registry: RUNNING)\"\n    description: \"LLaMA n=250 scaled cross-architecture validation — THE critical worst-tier experiment\"\n    expected_results:\n      imp_vs_rand_dz_s015: 0.11\n      imp_vs_rand_dz_s020: 0.14\n      imp_vs_rand_dz_s025: 0.17\n      imp_vs_rand_dz_s030: 0.19\n      bonferroni_significant_conditions: 0\n      phase_gradient_importance_dz_all: \">1.0 (robust)\"\n      phase_gradient_random_dz_all: \"0.30-0.45 (significant, CI excludes zero)\"\n      imp_vs_rand_monotonic: true\n      median_diff_s030: 0.18\n      median_diff_s030_ci: [-0.02, 0.38]\n    result_rationale: \"N=250 reveals that n=50 LLaMA result (d_z 0.34 at s030, Bonferroni p=0.029) was noise inflated. With 5× more data, the true d_z shrinks to ~0.19 — still positive (monotonic trend preserved) but entirely NS after Bonferroni correction (all 4 conditions p>0.05). Critically, within-importance phase gradient remains large (d_z>1.0) confirming phase modulation is robust, but imp_vs_rand d_z < 0.20 means strategy specificity is negligible on LLaMA architecture. Meanwhile, random phase gradient at d_z 0.30-0.45 with n=250 CI firmly excluding zero means random is ALSO phase-modulated on LLaMA. Interpretation: phase gradient is a universal compression phenomenon, not strategy-specific. The n=50 apparent significance was a false positive at the edge of the Bonferroni threshold.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: LLaMA n=250 imp_vs_rand d_z by sparsity, all NS (p>0.10 Bonferroni)\"\n      - \"Table: LLaMA random phase gradient d_z 0.30-0.45, all significant at n=250\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: LLaMA n=250 imp_vs_rand d_z with CI all crossing zero (or barely above)\"\n      - \"Comparison: DeepSeek imp_vs_rand d_z 0.44-0.80 vs LLaMA 0.11-0.19 — order of magnitude difference\"\n    analysis: \"This is the definitive worst-tier result. Strategy×phase interaction is architecture-specific: strong on Qwen2 (DeepSeek+Qwen), negligible on Llama. Core C1 framing ('strategy specificity is emergent') collapses to 'strategy specificity is an architecture-contingent phenomenon observed on Qwen2'. Paper must reframe: phase gradient is the universal finding, strategy modulation is one manifestation. Methodology contribution (II metric + phase-stratified analysis protocol) becomes the primary novelty.\"\n\n  - name: \"gpqa_ds_importance_s015\"\n    plan_id: \"gpqa_ds_importance_s015 (registry: RUNNING)\"\n    description: \"GPQA DeepSeek importance s015 — cross-benchmark hardest test\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 0.25\n      ii_high_median: 0.18\n      median_difference: 0.07\n      phase_gradient_monotonic: false\n      wilcoxon_p: 0.35\n      cohens_dz: 0.12\n      n_valid_problems: 35\n      mid_null_rate: 0.55\n    result_rationale: \"GPQA 是 hard science reasoning（physics/chemistry/biology），CoT 结构与 MATH-500 不同——更短、更 factual-retrieval oriented、less sequential computation。At s015 (lowest sparsity), compound interaction is expected to be weak even on MATH-500 (DS median_diff=0.39). On GPQA: (1) shorter CoT means less temporal structure → phase segmentation less meaningful (55% mid-null rate); (2) reasoning structure different from math → phase boundaries poorly align with actual cognitive demands; (3) at s015 the compression is too mild to trigger meaningful compound interaction on a different task type. Result: near-zero gradient, NS, non-monotonic because the signal is in the noise floor. The II values for high and low phases are within noise of each other because GPQA problems don't have the same 'exploration→computation→verification' phase structure that MATH-500 problems have.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: GPQA phase gradient vs MATH-500 at s015: DS MATH-500 median_diff=0.39 vs GPQA=0.07\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: GPQA phases showing flat/non-monotonic II pattern with overlapping CIs\"\n    analysis: \"GPQA s015 NS and non-monotonic. If s020 also fails, the cross-benchmark generalization story collapses: effect is MATH-500 specific (and partially GSM8K), not a general property of reasoning tasks.\"\n\n  - name: \"gpqa_ds_importance_s020\"\n    plan_id: \"gpqa_ds_importance_s020 (registry: QUEUED)\"\n    description: \"GPQA DeepSeek importance s020 — critical for decay trend\"\n    expected_results:\n      ii_low_median: 0.55\n      ii_high_median: 0.35\n      median_difference: 0.20\n      phase_gradient_monotonic: false\n      wilcoxon_p: 0.12\n      cohens_dz: 0.22\n      imp_rand_ratio_estimated: 1.3\n      n_valid_problems: 38\n      mid_null_rate: 0.50\n    result_rationale: \"S020 on GPQA: slightly larger effect than s015 (expected from dose-response) but still NS and weak. Key metric for worst tier: imp/rand ratio. If GPQA random at s020 produces median_diff ≈ 0.15 (extrapolating from LLaMA random behavior where random also shows phase gradient), then imp/rand ratio = 0.20/0.15 ≈ 1.3 — within the [0.8, 1.8] worst tier range. This confirms the decay trend: MATH-500 ratio 15-36× → GSM8K 2.3-3.8× → GPQA ≈ 1.0-1.5×. The gradient IS there (positive median_diff) but it's (a) weak, (b) not significant, (c) not specific to importance strategy. The CoT structure in GPQA (shorter chains, more knowledge retrieval) doesn't create the pronounced phase differentiation that MATH-500's long exploratory reasoning chains do.\"\n    tables:\n      - \"Table: Cross-benchmark imp/rand ratio decay — MATH-500: 15-36× | GSM8K: 2.3-3.8× | GPQA: ~1.3×\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Decay plot: strategy specificity ratio as function of benchmark/task type\"\n      - \"GPQA phase distribution showing high mid-null rate and weak phase separation\"\n    analysis: \"GPQA s020 confirms the worst-tier prediction: strategy specificity vanishes on tasks with different CoT structure. The paper's core finding is MATH-500 specific (where long sequential reasoning creates pronounced phases). Reframe: 'Phase-dependent heterogeneity is most pronounced in tasks requiring extended sequential computation (MATH-500, partially GSM8K) and attenuates on tasks with shorter/different reasoning structures (GPQA). This task-dependence is itself an important finding for the methodology framework—it identifies WHEN phase-stratified analysis is most informative'.\"\n\n  # --- Reviewer simulation ---\n\n  - name: \"reviewer_assessment\"\n    plan_id: \"meta-analysis\"\n    description: \"Simulated reviewer scores and objections under worst tier\"\n    expected_results:\n      reviewer_1_score: 2.5\n      reviewer_1_main_concern: \"Novelty insufficient — Physics of KV Cache (Mar 2026) already establishes phase-dependent compression behavior. This paper adds data points but no new theoretical insight.\"\n      reviewer_2_score: 3.0\n      reviewer_2_main_concern: \"Generalizability — effect is architecture-specific (fails on LLaMA) and task-specific (vanishes on GPQA). Scope too narrow for EMNLP.\"\n      reviewer_3_score: 2.5\n      reviewer_3_main_concern: \"Practical impact — mitigation pilot failed. Without actionable downstream benefit, the observation is academically interesting but not a contribution.\"\n      average_score: 2.67\n      novelty_challenged: 3\n      accept_probability: 0.10\n    result_rationale: \"In worst tier, all three reviewers challenge novelty from different angles. R1 focuses on prior work overlap (Physics of KV Cache covers phase-dependent behavior theoretically, HIES covers discrimination collapse empirically). R2 focuses on generalizability failure (LLaMA n=250 NS, GPQA ≈1×). R3 focuses on 'so what' (mitigation failed, no practical protocol validated). The combination is fatal for acceptance as a 'finding paper'. The reframe to 'methodology paper' (II metric + phase-stratified audit protocol) partially addresses R3 but doesn't fully resolve R1 (what's novel about proposing a metric?) or R2 (if the method only works on one architecture/benchmark, what's the point?). Average 2.67 with all three challenging novelty → reject with encouragement to resubmit after broader validation.\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Reframe strategy: (1) Position as 'complementary to Physics of KV Cache' not competing; (2) Emphasize methodology over finding; (3) Acknowledge task/architecture dependence as boundary condition, frame it as the secondary contribution (identifying when phase analysis matters). Accept probability 5-20%.\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6a75bff4-afe9-4dc7-a729-1c3fa93fc9a2","total_cost_usd":0.77376,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56698,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":14468,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56698,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":14468,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56698,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56698},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":51662,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.051767,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":14468,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":56698,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.721993,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"88468dda-a1f7-4843-89d4-a4161bf63393"}
